{"ts":1793391553218,"event":"done","summary":"PLAT-103 shipped. validateApp (libs/shared-contracts) now throws when app.owner is missing or blank; version bumped 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0 (breaking). Core shell (owner 'platform'), billing ('payments') and reports ('insights') each pass their owner, matching package.json team. Assumptions: (1) reports also calls validateApp, so I added it as PLAT-103-4 to keep its next deploy from crashing at startup; (2) owner values are hardcoded to match package.json team, since the inliner cannot import JSON; (3) the libs/ version bump is informational, since shared-contracts is inlined and never published. Merge order: PR #1 (contract), then #2 (billing), #3 (shell), #4 (reports). All CI and CD green. PR #1 landed alone briefly, but nothing deploys from libs/, so the live site was unaffected in that window."}
